  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1103 PM CDT SAT OCT 10 2026\n\nSatellite imagery this evening reveals the decaying swirl from\nPost Tropical Cyclone Isaias across Alabama. Lingering low level\nmoisture is resulting in a few pockets of light rain/drizzle and\nlow level clouds late this evening. This will likely be the theme\novernight with conditions gradually improving through the day\nSunday. Upper level ridging builds in early next week as the\nremnants of Isaias continue to move east-northeast. This will\nprovide a stretch of warm and dry weather across Central Alabama.\nHighs look to rebound into the low 90s by mid week with lows\ngenerally in the 50s/60s.\n\n95/Castillo",
